Original commit body from 1ab6cc8e83f39db1b0b6da6e0656c07a658d7fd7:

The default (hybrid) Configuration section depended on PYTHONHASHSEED on
any repo with more than 15 manifests. _collect_config_content iterated the
frozenset _MONOREPO_MANIFEST_NAMES and unsorted globs, and its discovery
caller iterated a set; _extract_config_embedding keeps the first 15
candidates that yield chunks and its first-pass cross-file dedup keeps the
first near-duplicate, so WHICH files were shown followed the str-hash salt
(three salts on a 32-manifest fixture -> three file sets). PR #1509 fixed
only the heuristic path.

- _MONOREPO_MANIFEST_NAMES is a tuple in CONFIG_FILES declaration order.
- Monorepo matches are gathered per kind and sorted (mirrors the heuristic).
- *-pattern globs, the discovered set, known_names and the rglob fallbacks
  in _discover_config_files_embedding / _get_repo_languages are sorted.
- Discovery compared unresolved paths against resolved seen_paths, so a
  manifest already collected was appended twice under a relative root
  (40 entries for 32 files); it now compares resolved paths.
- The 15-file cap is exercised by a test; its pragma is removed.
- Removed sketch_embeddings._get_repo_languages, an unreferenced duplicate
  of the sketch.py helper with the same unsorted-rglob early exit.

